{"name":"Nominee","hex":"#357567","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nominee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person named, or designated, by another, to any office, duty, or position; one nominated, or proposed, by others for office or for election to office.","A person or organisation in whose name a security is registered though true ownership is held by another party, called nominator, especially for the purpose of concealing the identity of the nominator."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nominee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candidate","blocks":[{"text":"A candidate, or nominee, is a prospective recipient of an award or honor, or a person seeking or being considered for some kind of position. For example, one can be a candidate for membership in a group or election to an office, in which case a candidate selection occurs."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candidate","wikidata":"Q618536"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg/500px-Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg/1280px-Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg/500px-Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACampaign_Signs_DSC02551_(1905616979).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/John_Turmel_at_Toronto-Danforth_2012_By-Election_Meeting.jpg/330px-John_Turmel_at_Toronto-Danforth_2012_By-Election_Meeting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa